 "description": "M26: a whole village over 30 days, starting at Hamlet, normal difficulty, threats (raids and sieges) on, weather fixed clear. Setup builds every building type on one 56 x 36 site (Village and Town buildings stay red until the tier) with a stone-age kit: 96 bread, planks, cobblestone, coal, stone tools, a bow, 32 emeralds, 12 adults. The scenario then plays a pretend player: day 1 it hires a farmer x2, a lumberjack and a cook; the standing orders (each runs once, when the tier allows it, and the hire is kept filled afterwards) hire a merchant, miner, hunter, two guards and a builder at Village and a blacksmith at Town. No other input. The roadmap criteria are the assertions: reaches Village, food days left is never 0 two dawns running, the treasury is never negative (VillageState rejects a negative purse, so this one cannot fail at L3: it is proven at L1 by PayRunTest), village logic under 1 ms a tick. Targets (tier_town, strikes, births) are reported in the summary, not asserted.",
